<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Remarkably, the Gemara continues and brings as its first example precisely our story: "Just as the Holy One, Blessed be He, visited the sick- as it says, 'And the Lord appeared to him in the plains of Mamre' \(Bereshit 18:1\)" - referring to God's visit to Abraham after his circumcision - "so too should you visit the sick." The divine revelation at the beginning of our parasha was itself an act of bikur holim, God visiting Abraham during his recovery!)
/E (Remarkably, the Gemara continues and brings as its first example precisely our story: "Just as the Holy One, Blessed be He, visited the sick- as it says, 'And the Lord appeared to him in the plains of Mamre' \(Bereshit 18:1\)" - referring to God's visit to Abraham after his circumcision - "so too should you visit the sick." The divine revelation at the beginning of our parasha was itself an act of bikur holim, God visiting Abraham during his recovery!)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [12 13]
