/T (For Abraham Abinu, therefore, the act of hospitality- of performing acts of kindness-was not a departure from standing before God. It was, in fact, a direct continuation of that very standing, and perhaps even a greater closeness to the Divine. By emulating God's ways of compassion and kindness, Abraham was not interrupting his communion with God; he was deepening it and proving that he had truly grasped its essence.)
/E (For Abraham Abinu, therefore, the act of hospitality- of performing acts of kindness-was not a departure from standing before God. It was, in fact, a direct continuation of that very standing, and perhaps even a greater closeness to the Divine. By emulating God's ways of compassion and kindness, Abraham was not interrupting his communion with God; he was deepening it and proving that he had truly grasped its essence.)
